course: dictionary
lesson: 3898
title: Friday, the day before the weekend
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Friday is one of the seven days of the week. It comes after Thursday and before Saturday. Days of the week start with a capital letter, so write Friday, not friday.
explain: For most children, Friday is the last day of the school week, and then the weekend starts. Some families have special Friday rules. In Manchester, «Friday rules, love» means Lyra can stay up later at Gran's, when bedtime is usually 8.
explain: The little word around Friday gives you clues. «On Friday» means one special day. «On Fridays» means every Friday, so the extra s means more than one. In maths, counting from Monday to Friday gives you 5 school days.
fact: Friday is a day of the week.
fact: Friday comes after Thursday and before Saturday.
fact: For most children, Friday is the last day of the school week.
fact: We write Friday with a capital F, and Fridays means every Friday.
fact: «TGIF» means «thank goodness it's Friday», which people say when the weekend is near.
exercise: Which day comes after Thursday? | Wednesday | *Friday | Sunday
exercise: For most children, which day is the last day of the school week? | Saturday | *Friday | Wednesday | Monday
exercise: Which word in «on Fridays at Gran's» means every Friday? | on | *Fridays | at | Gran's
test: Which day comes before Saturday? | *Friday | Sunday | Thursday
test: How many school days are there from Monday to Friday? | 3 | 2 | *5 | 7
exam: Which day comes after Friday, so that the weekend starts? | Monday | *Saturday | Wednesday | Thursday
